    <ObjectList>
      <MultilingualText ID="100000" CompositionName="Comment">
        <ObjectList>
          <MultilingualTextItem ID="100001" CompositionName="Items">
            <AttributeList>
              <Culture>en-US</Culture>
              <Text>EXAMPLE instance DB for FB_Valve - one valve, wired in examples/calling-network.ir. START VALUES ARE DOWNLOAD-TIME ONLY and every command member is overwritten by the caller each scan, so the values that actually matter here are the two SETTINGS: FTTime, which must cover this actuator's travel in its slower direction, and EnableUPSTime. Both ship non-zero on purpose - a zero fail-to time raises both faults during every legitimate transit. The whole struct is RETAIN, which is what C-132 makes possible and what keeps a latched fault alive across a power cycle; note that this retains the entire interface, not only the latched causes.</Text>
            </AttributeList>
          </MultilingualTextItem>
        </ObjectList>
      </MultilingualText>
